<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Spurius Cassius Vecellinus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 485 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Spurius Cassius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Spurius Cassius Vecellinus was a Roman statesman of the early Republic, three times consul. In 493 BCE he concluded the treaty with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> League known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/foedus-cassianum">Foedus Cassianum</a>, which made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latins">Latins</a> equal allies for mutual defence. According to tradition he proposed the first agrarian law in 486 BCE and was executed the next year, accused of seeking to make himself king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/spurius-cassius-vecellinus.jpg" alt="Spurius Cassius Vecellinus" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Domenico Beccafumi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Domenico_Beccafumi_009.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
